@startuml GupShup Cafe - English Feedback Flow Sequence

' Use latest PlantUML version features
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1976D2
}

title GupShup Cafe - English Feedback Modal Flow (Real-time Feedback)

participant "User\n(Alice)" as Alice
participant "React App" as React
participant "AudioContext" as Audio
participant "Socket.io" as Socket
participant "Backend\n(FastAPI)" as Backend
participant "AWS Strands\nOrchestrator" as Orchestrator
participant "EnglishAgent" as Agent
participant "Database" as DB

== Speaking Turn Begins ==

Alice -> React : Speaking turn starts
React -> React : Timer begins (60s)
React -> Audio : Enable speaking
Audio --> Alice : Mic active indicator

== Real-time Transcription ==

Alice -> Audio : Speaks: "I thinks artificial\nintelligence is very good"
Audio -> Audio : Capture audio stream

note over React
    Web Speech API
    running in browser
end note

React -> React : SpeechRecognition.start()
React -> React : Got interim transcript:\n"I thinks artificial..."

React --> Alice : Show live transcript\nin SpeechToText panel

React -> React : Got final transcript:\n"I thinks artificial\nintelligence is very good"

React -> Socket : emit('speech-transcript', {\n  text: "I thinks...",\n  speaker: "Alice",\n  timestamp: Date.now()\n})

Socket -> Backend : speech-transcript event

== Backend Processing ==

Backend -> DB : INSERT transcript
DB --> Backend : transcript_id

Backend -> Backend : Prepare for instant feedback
Backend -> Backend : Get previous feedback\nfor context

Backend -> DB : SELECT recent_feedback\nWHERE participant_id = Alice
DB --> Backend : previous_feedback: [...]

Backend -> Orchestrator : get_english_feedback({\n  statements: [{\n    speaker: "Alice",\n    text: "I thinks..."\n  }],\n  instant: true,\n  context: {\n    topic: "AI Technology",\n    previous_feedback: [...],\n    participant_name: "Alice"\n  }\n})

== Instant Grammar Analysis ==

note over Orchestrator
    Instant mode: 2-3 second target
end note

Orchestrator -> Agent : analyze({\n  text: "I thinks artificial...",\n  mode: "instant"\n})

Agent -> Agent : **Quick Grammar Check**\nIssue found:\n"I thinks" → subject-verb error

Agent -> Agent : **Quick Vocabulary Check**\n"artificial intelligence" - good\n"very good" - basic adjective

Agent -> Agent : **Quick Fluency Check**\nSentence structure: clear\nNo major pauses

Agent -> Agent : **Calculate Scores**\n- Grammar: 6/10 (1 error)\n- Vocabulary: 7/10 (basic)\n- Fluency: 8/10 (smooth)\n- Overall: 7.0/10

Agent -> Agent : **Determine CEFR**\nScore 7.0 → B1 level

Agent --> Orchestrator : {\n  grammar_score: 6,\n  grammar_issues: [{\n    original: "I thinks",\n    corrected: "I think",\n    reason: "subject-verb agreement",\n    severity: "high"\n  }],\n  vocabulary_score: 7,\n  vocabulary_level: "intermediate",\n  fluency_score: 8,\n  cefr_level: "B1",\n  overall_score: 7.0\n}

== Format Feedback for UI ==

Orchestrator -> Orchestrator : _format_feedback_message(result)

note over Orchestrator
    Creates user-friendly message:
    
    📝 Grammar Feedback:
    ⚠ "I thinks" → "I think"
       (subject-verb agreement)
    
    ✓ Rest is clear!
end note

Orchestrator -> Orchestrator : _format_gentle_mention(Alice, result)

note over Orchestrator
    Creates agent mention:
    
    "Alice, great point!
    Quick tip: 'I think'
    instead of 'I thinks'"
end note

Orchestrator --> Backend : {\n  success: true,\n  speaker: "Alice",\n  feedback_type: "instant",\n  response_time: "2-3s",\n  grammar: {\n    score: 6,\n    issues: [...],\n    suggestions: [...]\n  },\n  vocabulary: {\n    score: 7,\n    level: "intermediate"\n  },\n  fluency: {\n    score: 8,\n    comments: "Smooth delivery"\n  },\n  cefr_level: "B1",\n  overall_score: 7.0,\n  display_message: "📝 Grammar...",\n  agent_mention: "Alice, great point!..."\n}

== Store Feedback ==

Backend -> DB : INSERT feedback ({\n  session_id: "...",\n  participant_id: "Alice",\n  feedback_type: "instant",\n  grammar_score: 6,\n  vocabulary_score: 7,\n  fluency_score: 8,\n  cefr_level: "B1",\n  display_message: "...",\n  created_at: now()\n})

DB --> Backend : feedback_id

== Send to User (Private) ==

note over Backend
    Emit only to Alice's socket
    (private feedback)
end note

Backend -> Socket : emit('english-feedback',\n  feedback,\n  room=alice_socket_id\n)

Socket -> React : 'english-feedback' event

== Display Feedback Modal ==

React -> React : EnglishFeedbackModal state update

note over React
    Modal appears bottom-right
    with feedback data
end note

React --> Alice : **English Feedback Modal**\n\n**CEFR: B1** Score: 7.0/10\n\n📝 Grammar Feedback:\n⚠ "I thinks" → "I think"\n   (subject-verb agreement)\n✓ Rest is clear!\n\n**Vocabulary**: 7/10\n**Fluency**: 8/10

Alice -> React : Reads feedback
Alice -> React : Continues speaking

note over Alice
    Feedback shown privately,
    other participants
    don't see it
end note

== Optional: Agent Mention ==

note over Backend
    Optionally, agent can
    mention feedback gently
    in the discussion
end note

Backend -> Socket : emit('agent-message', {\n  text: "Alice, great point!\\n  Quick tip: 'I think'\\n  instead of 'I thinks'",\n  speaker: "Alice"\n})

Socket -> React : 'agent-message' event
React --> Alice : Display in chat area

== Dismiss Modal ==

Alice -> React : Click X or wait 10s
React -> React : Auto-dismiss modal
React --> Alice : Modal closes

== End of Turn ==

React -> React : Timer expires (60s)
React -> Socket : emit('end-turn')
Socket -> Backend : end-turn event

Backend -> Backend : Move to next speaker
Backend -> Socket : emit('turn-started', {\n  current_speaker_index: 1\n})

Socket -> React : Update UI
React --> Alice : Next speaker highlighted

note as FeedbackUIDesign
    **English Feedback Modal Design:**
    
    **Position**: Bottom-right, non-blocking
    **Timing**: Appears 2-3 seconds after speaking
    **Duration**: 10 seconds auto-dismiss, or manual close
    **Privacy**: Only visible to the speaker
    **Content**:
    1. CEFR Level badge (colored)
    2. Overall score (X/10)
    3. Grammar issues with corrections
    4. Vocabulary score + level
    5. Fluency score + comments
    6. Top suggestions (actionable)
    
    **Separate from SpeechToText Tab**:
    - SpeechToText: Shows live transcript
    - English Feedback Modal: Shows AI analysis
    - Both can be open simultaneously
    
    **User Experience**:
    - Non-intrusive (doesn't block discussion)
    - Quick glance feedback
    - Detailed enough to be actionable
    - Encourages self-correction
    
    **Real-time Flow**:
    1. User speaks (WebRTC audio to others)
    2. Browser transcribes (Web Speech API)
    3. Transcript sent to backend
    4. LLM analyzes in 2-3 seconds
    5. Private feedback shown in modal
    6. User continues discussion
    
    **Comprehensive Feedback**:
    After discussion ends, user gets:
    - Full session analysis
    - CEFR progress tracking
    - Detailed recommendations
    - Comparison across turns
end note

@enduml
